      "author": "Hollowmere team",
      "story": "Arvid Lindqvist ran beaver and marten sets along the Tamsin from this one-room cabin for twenty-six winters. In November something that had been a man started robbing his sets; Arvid lost a hand finding out what it was. He put his good things in the cache box at the foot of his bunk, hung its key in the smokehouse where he kept everything he could not afford to lose, and when the fever came he told the Rask boys from down the river what to do. They nailed his door shut from outside and wrote on it. Later Jory Rask went back in through the wall under the lean-to, to bury him; he is still sitting at the table. Arvid's sets are still out in the yard and along the path, the way the journal says.",
